.TH REXAMP 1 2026-10-21 "rexamp 3.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rexamp \- terminal music player for Plex Media Server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rexamp
.RB [ \-\-log\-level
.IR level ]
.br
.B rexamp login
.br
.B rexamp logout
.br
.B rexamp switch
.RI [ library ]
.br
.B rexamp
.BR \-\-version " | " \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rexamp
plays the music library on your Plex Media Server from the terminal.
Run without a subcommand, it opens the player.
On first run it signs in to Plex and asks which server and music library to use.
.PP
The queue and volume are saved between sessions.
When D\-Bus (Linux) or Control Center (macOS) is available,
.B rexamp
also responds to media keys and system media controls.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B login
Sign in to Plex and choose a server and music library.
.B rexamp
prints a URL; open it in a browser and sign in.
It waits up to five minutes for the sign\-in to finish.
Signing in forgets the previously chosen server and library.
.TP
.B logout
Forget the saved Plex tokens.
.TP
.BR switch " [\fIlibrary\fR]"
Choose another music library from any reachable server on the account.
Without an argument, lists the libraries and asks which to use.
With
.IR library ,
a 1\-based index into that list, picks it directly.
Switching library clears the saved queue.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level " level"
Log verbosity: one of
.BR trace ", " debug ", " info ", " warn ", " error .
Defaults to
.BR info .
See
.BR FILES .
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.SH INTERFACE
The window has a sidebar of sections, a list of the selected section,
and a player.
.B Tab
moves focus between the sidebar and the list.
The bottom line shows the keys available in the current view.
Press
.B ?
for the full list of keybindings.
.PP
The sections are
.BR Artists ", " Albums ", " Playlists ", " Search " and " Queue .
.SH KEYS
.SS Navigation
.TP 18
.BR j ", " Down
Move down.
.TP
.BR k ", " Up
Move up.
.TP
.BR g ", " Home
Go to the top.
.TP
.BR G ", " End
Go to the bottom.
.TP
.BR Ctrl\-d ", " PgDn
Half page down.
.TP
.BR Ctrl\-u ", " PgUp
Half page up.
.TP
.BR l ", " Right ", " Enter
Open the selected item.
.TP
.BR h ", " Left ", " Backspace ", " Esc
Go back.
.TP
.B Tab
Toggle focus between sidebar and list.
.TP
.BR 1 \(en 5
Jump to Artists, Albums, Playlists, Search or Queue.
.TP
.B /
Search.
In the search field,
.B Enter
searches and
.B Esc
cancels.
.SS Lists
.TP 18
.B P
Play now, replacing the queue.
.TP
.B S
Play shuffled, replacing the queue.
.TP
.B a
Add to the end of the queue.
.TP
.B n
Play next.
.SS Queue
.TP 18
.B d
Remove the selected track.
.TP
.B D
Clear the queue.
.TP
.B J
Move the selected track down.
.TP
.B K
Move the selected track up.
.SS Player
These work from any view.
.TP 18
.B Space
Play or pause.
.TP
.B >
Next track.
.TP
.B <
Previous track, or restart the current one.
.TP
.B .
Seek forward 10 seconds.
.TP
.B ,
Seek back 10 seconds.
.TP
.B +
Volume up.
.TP
.B \-
Volume down.
.TP
.B s
Toggle shuffle.
.TP
.B r
Cycle repeat: off, all, one.
.TP
.B m
Toggle the player between maximized and minimized.
.TP
.B c
Cast to a device.
Only in builds with the
.B cast
feature.
.TP
.B ?
Show help.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH CASTING
Builds with the
.B cast
feature can play to Google Cast devices.
Press
.B c
to pick a device; while casting, the volume keys control the device's own volume.
Devices are found with mDNS, unless
.B static_cast_devices
is set in the configuration file, in which case only those devices are offered.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B rexamp
reads
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rexamp/config.toml ,
by default
.IR ~/.config/rexamp/config.toml .
The file and every key in it are optional.
.TP
.B accent_color
Color for focus, selection and highlights.
A color name such as
.B cyan
or
.BR light\-blue ,
a 256\-color index such as
.BR 208 ,
or a hex color such as
.BR #ff8800 .
Defaults to
.BR cyan .
.TP
.B static_cast_devices
An array of tables with
.B name
and
.B ip
keys.
When set, these devices are offered for casting instead of discovering devices with mDNS.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
accent_color = "cyan"

[[static_cast_devices]]
name = "Living Room TV"
ip = "192.168.1.20"
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/rexamp/config.toml
Configuration, see
.BR CONFIGURATION .
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/rexamp/state.json
Saved state: Plex tokens, chosen server and library, volume and queue.
Written with mode 0600.
Versions 1.5 and earlier kept the login and server keys in
.IR config.toml ;
.B rexamp
copies them here on first start, after which they can be removed from
.IR config.toml .
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/rexamp/rexamp.YYYY\-MM\-DD.log
Log files, rotated daily; the last three are kept.
.PP
On macOS these files live in
.IR ~/Library/Application\ Support/rexamp/ .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, non\-zero on error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Sign in and open the player:
.PP
.RS
.B rexamp
.RE
.PP
Use the second music library without being asked:
.PP
.RS
.B rexamp switch 2
.RE
.PP
Run with verbose logging:
.PP
.RS
.B rexamp \-\-log\-level debug
.RE
